11. What the analyst score means

The analyst ranking is an extension of the paper.

The paper itself does not publish a "best analyst" ranking.

The project uses information such as:

Accuracy

How small the analyst's historical absolute forecast errors are.

Consistency

How stable the analyst's errors or unexplained residuals are.

Freshness

How recently the analyst revised the estimate before the scoring
snapshot.

Evidence

How much history supports the score.

Credibility weighting reduces the influence of analysts with very few
observations. The model uses:

n observations / (n observations + credibility prior)

The credibility prior is configured in src/config.py.

A great result from one or two observations should therefore not
automatically outrank a strong analyst with a much longer history.

