13. What the Fama regression is testing

The main strategy analysis is not intended to be an FF5 regression for
one company.

The intended flow is:

many companies
    |
analyst forecast errors
    |
analyst models and sentiment
    |
company consensus
    |
Fama French industry aggregation
    |
Long Short industry strategy
    |
monthly strategy returns
    |
FF5 regression

The pure FF5 regression is conceptually:

Strategy excess return
=
alpha
+ market factor
+ size factor
+ value factor
+ profitability factor
+ investment factor
+ residual

The strategy timing is designed conservatively so a quarterly signal is
used for the next eligible monthly return rather than earning a return
from information that was not yet available.

14. Why a single company will usually not produce an FF5 strategy result

This is expected.

The strategy uses five Long industries and five Short industries. It
therefore needs at least ten valid industries in a period.

It also needs enough analyst history for the expanding window analyst
models.

A single ticker such as CME or TSM cannot provide that universe.

A warning such as:

No Long-Short returns could be constructed

does not automatically mean the FF5 code is broken. It usually means the
current dataset does not contain enough industry coverage or trainable
analyst history.

15. Combine companies without using FactSet again

This is important when API usage is limited.

If company CSVs already exist in outputs/, use --from-outputs.

Example:

py -3.11 master_pipeline.py --from-outputs --tickers AAPL-US,APO-US,CME-US,EME-US,GFS-US,GME-US,GS-US,KLAC-US,NBIS-US,NRG-US,TSM-US --factor-model FF5 --factor-backtest

This mode reads the existing CSV files and makes zero FactSet API calls.

Do not type ... in the ticker list. Every entry is interpreted as an
actual ticker.

The master analysis can create files such as:

master_raw_forecast_errors.csv
master_raw_estimates.csv
master_raw_actuals.csv
master_raw_prices.csv
master_consensus.csv
master_industry_sentiment.csv
master_analyst_scores.csv
master_ff_factors.csv
master_strategy_returns.csv
master_factor_regression.csv
master_run_info.csv

Factor output files are only produced when the strategy has enough data
to construct valid returns and run the regression.

16. How to know whether the multi company dataset is large enough

Watch these lines in the terminal:

input panel
expanding-window NN/linear predictions
industries seen
analyst reliability scores computed

For example, a run with many raw observations can still be too small if
only one analyst has enough history to generate a valid model
prediction.

The current goal is not simply "more rows."

You want:

More companies.

More distinct Fama French industries.

Analysts who cover multiple companies.

More quarters of analyst history.

Many valid expanding window predictions.

For the five Long and five Short strategy, ten industries is the
mathematical minimum. A larger universe is preferable.

17. Recommended workflow for adding companies

When adding a larger universe:

Check which company CSVs already exist.

Never repull a company just because you want it in the master
analysis.

Pull only missing companies.

Watch the FactSet daily request limit.

After each batch, rerun the zero API master analysis.

Check whether industry coverage and valid NN predictions improved.

Continue until the strategy has enough data.

List existing company forecast error files with:

Get-ChildItem outputs\live_*_raw_forecast_errors.csv | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Name

18. SIC codes and Fama French industries

The project maps company SIC codes into the Fama French 48 industry
classification.

For US companies, the pipeline can use SEC EDGAR to resolve SIC codes
without using a FactSet request.

Manual overrides can be placed in TICKER_SIC_OVERRIDES in
src/config.py when necessary.

