20. Common problems

"Python version 2.7 does not support an F prefix"

The wrong Python interpreter is being used.

Use:

py -3.11 ...

PowerShell says def, from, or Python variables are not recognized

Python source code was pasted directly into PowerShell.

Open a fresh terminal and run only the commands shown in the PowerShell
examples.

cd fails because of "Analyst Model code"

The path contains spaces. Use quotation marks:

cd "C:\Users\patri\Documents\Analyst Model code\analyst-model"

py_compile returns nothing

That is success.

No Long-Short returns could be constructed

Usually insufficient industry coverage or insufficient analyst model
history.

Factor CSV files do not appear

The factor backtest did not produce a valid strategy result. The Excel
exporter cannot create meaningful factor result sheets until those
underlying strategy outputs exist.

FactSet daily request limit exceeded

Stop live pulls. Existing output analysis remains available with
--from-outputs.

Shares outstanding contains a FactSet error

The data cleaning layer treats known FactSet FQL error strings as
missing shares data. A valid direct market capitalization can still be
used when FactSet provides it.

